<title>LITHUANIA: CENTRAL BANK SAYS 1996 PROFIT 72.5 MLN LITAS.</title>
<headline>CENTRAL BANK SAYS 1996 PROFIT 72.5 MLN LITAS.</headline>
<text>
<p>VILNIUS, March 20 - Lithuania's central bank said on Thursday that its 1996 profit was 72.5 million litas.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that under the law it would divide the profit 20 percent to its share capital, 50 percent to the reserve capital and 30 percent to the state budget.</p>
</text>
